  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Viet Nam - Cyclone Typhoon Yagi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation targets the most vulnerable communities, including 130,000 people across seven northern provinces, prioritizing households that have lost their livelihoods, suffered significant damage, or are particularly vulnerable (e.g., elderly, disabled).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The response focuses on the seven northern provinces of Vietnam most affected by Typhoon Yagi: Lao Cai, Yen Bai, Cao Bang, Phu Tho, Thai Nguyen, Bac Giang, and Lang Son.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The response includes immediate relief, multi-purpose cash grants, and shelter repair assistance, along with longer-term recovery efforts like livelihood restoration, WASH, and health interventions. VNRC coordinates with local and international partners to mobilize resources and deploy relief items, cash, and support.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The response is driven by the severe impact of Typhoon Yagi in Vietnam, which caused widespread destruction, loss of life, and significant displacement. The operation aims to address urgent humanitarian needs and support recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Viet Nam - Cyclone Typhoon Yagi</narrative>
  </description>
